    "New BFD objecte73515d0/5240B is a newly compiled artifact, distinct from prior SDK21 object3000b4e7/5296B. It defines exactly four global FUNC BFD bridges (upper10B/canonicalize13B each) and no undefined imports. Both genuine linked executables have exactly one Rust main and their two expected bridges. Actual259B layout e21b4d99 matches the accepted typed header ABI witness: BFDxvec8, upper504, canonicalize512, bfd304/align8, target904/align8. This is artifact/ABI evidence, not new runtime behavior.",
    "Both x86_64 ELF64 executables are ET_DYN with interpreter/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 and DT_FLAGS_1 PIE. Each carries GNU_PROPERTY note type0xc0008002/data07000000 and Linux ABI3.2.0; build IDs are710f4a2ab941499ea2da06fe912cc48549581c9a and6d98bf4b90285665c67ef4d4e6c21553550c3ea3. These are actual compatibility witnesses, not new kernel/app execution.",
    "Pinned Rocky libbfd.so is a real linker input resolving libbfd.a/libsframe/libiberty in actual link.d. Both binaries contain actual local bfd_openr, bfd_check_format, bfd_get_error and bfd_errmsg providers. The absence of DT_NEEDED libbfd is explained by that recorded static library resolution; no BFD callback/test double is substituted.",
